   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653",
   "widgets_values": [
    "### PixelArtistry · Split a character into parts (Qwen Image 2.1 edit)\n\n1. Crop **one part** from your character image (head, body, cloth, arm, leg) and load it in **Load Image**.\n2. Paste the matching prompt from `prompts/` and adjust it to your character.\n3. Run. The output keeps the input's size and camera.\n\n- The crop goes into `image_1` of *Text Encode Qwen Image 2.1*; its latent sets the size.\n- Seed **56** (fixed), 25 steps, cfg 1, euler / simple. Reference resolution 1024 (1536 for the full body).\n- Prompt pattern: *what to keep* + *what to remove* + *strict front view, plain white background*.\n- Each part should bring what hides its seam: the whole beard for the head, the wrap for arms and legs."
   ]
  }
